 "text": "Hello, what's up? That' a good question. The reason is that the pigments and paints in acrylic paintings are more likely to be absorbed into the canvas when it's still wet. That's why. So when the painting dries, the pigments are stuck on the surface and don't absorb as much. Yeah, you can try out a few different paints and see how they look on the canvas. In that case, you can use a glossier paint or a lacquer, but be careful not to use too much, as it can make the painting too shiny and difficult to apply.",
